From 4fa021e323ad502f861f0cf81287e1379fd7e599 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Bruni <luca.bruni@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:20:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] gfx9-win: EXPERIMENTAL
 dxg-gfx9-isolate-internal-queue-on-compute1

Opt-in prototype, not for upstream as is.

gfx9 KMDs serialise contexts that share a WDDM node, so a kernel that waits on
another queue's progress, or on a runtime blit such as a code object upload,
deadlocks until the watchdog fires. Put the runtime's first compute queue (its
internal blit queue) alone on COMPUTE1 so uploads run while a user kernel
occupies COMPUTE0. Only for gfx9 without HWS and when the KMD exposes
COMPUTE1.

Validated at the 7.15 nightly pin on gfx90c: 4 mempool hip-tests fixed, 0
regressions. Rebased onto the current pin: also skipped under ROCR_USE_PM4=1,
which upstream (#11068) pins to COMPUTE0; COMPUTE1 id moved next to
kSchedulerIdCompute0. Not rebuilt or retested after the rebase.
